 away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 29% clears the cost of capital of 9.2% by 20pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.84).","It converts 1% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.02x.","ROE of 34% is amplified by 5.5x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.6x net debt to EBITDA ($1.2B of cash against $2.1B of debt), with interest covered 12.5x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 9.9% over 3 years, 14.9% over 5 years and 8.5% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 18%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 29.1% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Capex runs 2.5x depreciation (9.2% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 16, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 13.1% on average.","Analysts expect 15.6% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (39 sales, net $14.4M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.8% (1.8% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.2% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 17,495 employees, each generates about $661K of revenue, 1.7x the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 8.3% a year.","That works out to $10K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $6.3M (10x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $6K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":61,"head":"Watch: priced 52% above its $163 fair value, but that value is low-confidence and the price is inside i